From: qin46xia
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: relearn aged SOE entries

The PPE ages an idle SOE entry back to UNBIND, but its flow keeps the
bound flag and airoha_soe_ppe_flow_bind_start() rejects bound flows, so
the entry was held unbound from then on. After a pause longer than the
bind age the whole SA (decrypt) or connection (encrypt) stayed on the
look-aside path, at about 220 Mbit/s.

Clear the stale binding when an unbound entry is learned again so it is
rebound through the normal completion barrier.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
index 429576e..0735206 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -2332,6 +2332,14 @@ static void airoha_ppe_foe_insert_entry(struct airoha_ppe *ppe,
 	}
 	if (hwe_bound && !soe_entry)
 		goto unlock;
+	/* The hardware ages an idle SOE entry back to UNBIND while its flow
+	 * still counts as bound, and bind_start() refuses a bound flow. That
+	 * left the SA (and every flow sharing it) on the slow path for good
+	 * once traffic paused for the bind age. Forget the stale binding so
+	 * the entry is learned again through the normal completion barrier.
+	 */
+	if (!hwe_bound && soe_entry)
+		airoha_soe_ppe_flow_unbind(&soe_entry->soe_flow);
 
 	hlist_for_each_entry_safe(e, n, &ppe->foe_flow[index], list) {
 		bool bind_started = false;
-- 
